.TH GO-DHCPD-MIGRATION-TOOL 8 "October 2026" "go-dhcpd 1.8.0" "System Administration Commands"
.SH NAME
go-dhcpd-migration-tool \- migrate go-dhcpd subnets and static hosts from config.json5 into a sqlite3-config database
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B go-dhcpd-migration-tool
.RB \-c | \-\-config
.I file
.RB \-d | \-\-database
.I file
.RB [ \-n | \-\-dry\-run ]
.br
.B go-dhcpd-migration-tool
.RB { \-h | \-\-help }
.br
.B go-dhcpd-migration-tool
.RB { \-v | \-\-version }
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B go-dhcpd-migration-tool
is an offline, one-shot utility that migrates the
.B subnets
and
.B static
arrays from a go-dhcpd JSON5 configuration file into a
.BR sqlite3-config (8)
plugin database, creating the database file and schema if needed.
.PP
It operates directly on the SQLite database file through the same storage
and validation code used by the
.B sqlite3-config
plugin; the go-dhcpd daemon, its REST API, and the plugin process itself
are not involved and do not need to be running. This makes the tool
suitable for preparing a database ahead of switching an existing
deployment's
.B plugins.config_provider.name
from
.B file-config
to
.B sqlite3-config
without downtime.
.PP
Subnets and static hosts are each validated and migrated independently:
a validation or insertion failure in one record is reported and skipped,
it does not abort migration of the remaining records in either set.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIfile\fR
Path to the go-dhcpd
.B config.json5
file to read. Required.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-database " " \fIfile\fR
Path to the sqlite3 database file to create or update. Required. If the
file does not already exist it is created, along with its schema.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Validate the configuration's subnets and static hosts without opening or
writing to the database. Reports what would be migrated.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a usage summary, then exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the tool name and go-dhcpd version, then exit.
.SH OUTPUT
For each subnet and static host, the tool prints one of the following
progress lines to standard output:
.TP
.B [OK]
.RI ( \-\-dry\-run " only) the record passed validation and would be migrated."
.TP
.B [MIGRATED]
The record passed validation and was written to the database.
.TP
.B [INVALID]
The record failed validation (printed to standard error) and was not
migrated.
.TP
.B [FAILED]
The record passed validation but could not be inserted into the database
(printed to standard error), e.g. due to a duplicate key or database
error.
.PP
A summary line reporting the number of succeeded and failed records is
printed after each of the subnet and static-host migration passes.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Every subnet and static host was successfully validated (and, unless
.BR \-\-dry\-run " was given, migrated)."
.TP
.B 1
Configuration loading failed, the database could not be opened or
created, or one or more subnets or static hosts failed validation or
insertion.
.TP
.B 2
Required arguments were missing:
.B \-\-config
and/or
.B \-\-database
were not given.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I config.json5
Source configuration file, named by
.BR \-\-config .
Only its
.B subnets
and
.B static
arrays are read; all other sections (global, auth, plugins) are ignored.
.TP
.IR database " (named by " \-\-database )
Destination SQLite3 database, created with the same schema used by the
.B sqlite3-config
plugin. See
.BR go\-dhcpd\-sqlite3\-config (3).
.SH EXAMPLES
Validate a configuration without writing anything:
.PP
.RS
go-dhcpd-migration-tool \-\-config /etc/go-dhcpd/config.json5 \e
  \-\-database /var/lib/go-dhcpd/networks.db \-\-dry\-run
.RE
.PP
Migrate subnets and static hosts into a new or existing database:
.PP
.RS
go-dhcpd-migration-tool \-c /etc/go-dhcpd/config.json5 \e
  \-d /var/lib/go-dhcpd/networks.db
.RE
.PP
After migrating, point
.B plugins.config_provider
at
.B sqlite3-config
with
.B db_path
set to the migrated database, then restart
.BR dhcpd (8).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dhcpd (8),
.BR go\-dhcpd\-sqlite3\-config (3),
.BR go\-dhcpd\-file\-config (3),
.BR go\-dhcpd\-config.json5 (5)
